cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite both the artifact and the paper it accompanies."
title: "Answering Less to Score More: code and data artifact"
abstract: >-
  Complete replication archive for a measurement-validity audit of abstain-exclude
  fitness in prompt optimization: the experiment pipeline as run, the full run archive
  (146,550 raw model outputs, per-item strict and lenient predictions, generation logs,
  per-run configuration snapshots with model digests for the optimization runs), a separate
  105-check verifier that re-derives the main tables and selected textual statistics, separate
  reconstruction inputs for the escape-vector battery and the model screen, and the figure
  generation code. Component-specific licensing and the third-party-text exception are
  documented in DATA.md.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Çetinkaya"
    given-names: "Ali"
    email: "ali.cetinkaya@selcuk.edu.tr"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7747-6854"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Engineering, Faculty of Technology, Selçuk University, Konya, Türkiye"
# No root `license:` field: this is a mixed code-and-data deposit. Code is MIT, the author's
# derived data is CC BY 4.0, and no rights are claimed in third-party text incidentally
# reproduced in raw model outputs. CFF 1.2 reads a list of licenses as OR, not as
# component-specific terms, so per-component licensing is documented in DATA.md instead.
keywords:
